    Bug 1982288 - Fix test by disabling inline spell checking to prevent fails on early context menus. r=freaktechnik

    There is a fail in `MsgComposeCommands.js` which prevents the inline spell checker
    to be disabled according to `mail.spellcheck.inline` as defined in browser.toml [1].

    > 0:08.20 GECKO(68878) JavaScript error: chrome://messenger/content/messengercompose/MsgComposeCommands.js, line 7909: TypeError: can't access property "incomingServer", account is null
    > 0:08.21 GECKO(68878) JavaScript error: chrome://messenger/content/messengercompose/MsgComposeCommands.js, line 11285: NS_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED: Component returned failure code: 0xc1f30001 (NS_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED) [nsIMsgCompose.initEditor]

    The call for `enableInlineSpellCheck()` [2] is then never reached. This is fixed
    by adding an account in the test.

    Running with enabled inline spell checker causes other issues for context menus
    being opened quickly after composer startup, which are described in the bug as
    well [3], which may be addressed in a follow-up bug.

    [1]: https://searchfox.org/comm-central/source/mail/components/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml#5
    [2]: https://searchfox.org/comm-central/rev/f2f3f0a3a383f439facbcc7b2d50d0b852d549ba/mail/components/compose/content/MsgComposeCommands.js#11294-11295
    [3]: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1982288#c11

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D276473

